Calls down 356→113 but FPS unchanged 3.7. Something else is bottleneck! Maybe shadow map passes are not counted. Shadow map with 14 lights? Only directional casts shadow by default, point lights no castShadow. Shadow map at 2048 with 544 castShadow objects could be huge; after merge maybe 380 removed but merged 24 cast; other 160 children meshes (enemy etc) maybe. During menu no enemies. Still 3.7. Could be not graphics at all; maybe screenshot/headless throttle? Wait requestAnimationFrame under Playwright headless may be throttled to ~4fps because browser background/occluded window? Headless frames can be throttled? Normally headless RAF 60. We measured 3.7. CSS transition loader took a long time, consistent. Could be renderer actually not taking 250ms? Let's measure JS work per frame with `performance.now` around renderer.render by monkeypatching? We can wrap renderer.render and accumulate durations without modifying game loop. Since animate calls renderer.render; monkeypatch at runtime:
```
const orig = renderer.render.bind(renderer);
renderer.render = (...a)=>{const t=performance.now(); const r=orig(...a); window._r += performance.now()-t; window._c++; return r;}
```
